{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"ancient-domestic-orca","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# The DC harness's store-copy fixture hard-fails on `git fetch origin tickets` and swallows git's reason\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nLive External Integration run **31587452003** (2026-08-12, head `b13173bb7d`) ended the DC\nharness at `1 failed, 59 passed, 1 xfailed, 1 error in 2471.11s`. The **error** is a fixture\nfailure, not a cell defect:\n\n    ERROR tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py::test_outbound_unassign_round_trips\n      - subprocess.CalledProcessError: Command '['git','fetch','origin','tickets']'\n        returned non-zero exit status 128.\n\nIt aborts at setup of `dc_store_copy_repo` (`tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_fixtures.py:139`),\nwhich fetches the live `tickets` branch in the outer CI checkout and then `git archive\nFETCH_HEAD | tar -x` to seed a scrubbed store copy.\n\n**Two distinct problems, and the second is why the first is still unexplained:**\n\n1. **The fetch is a single un-retried network call on the critical path of a 41-minute live\n   job.** Any transient failure — a blip, a rate-limited GitHub, or a refspec/partial-clone\n   interaction (the CI checkout is a partial clone per epic 42eb, and `git fetch <remote>\n   <branch>` writing no remote-tracking ref under a narrow refspec is a known family — see the\n   closed bug `scorpioid-important-thylacine`) — takes the cell out as an ERROR.\n\n2. **The failure is undiagnosable, by construction.** The call is\n   `subprocess.run(..., capture_output=True, check=True)`: `capture_output=True` sends git's\n   stderr into a captured buffer, and `check=True` then raises `CalledProcessError` whose\n   string form carries only the exit status. Git's actual message — the one line that would\n   say whether this was auth, a missing ref, a refspec miss, or a network error — is\n   discarded. Reading the run log, exit 128 is all there is; the cause cannot be determined\n   after the fact. This is the same \"swallowed diagnostic\" shape the harness has been bitten\n   by before.\n\n## Approach\n\nFix the diagnostic first, because it is what makes the retry policy decidable.\n\n* Replace `check=True` on that fetch (and the `git archive` beside it, which has the same\n  shape) with an explicit check that raises with git's captured `stderr` in the message —\n  naming the command, the exit status, and the remote/branch.\n* Then make the fetch tolerate a transient failure: bounded retries with backoff, and on\n  final failure fail with the git message rather than a bare status. Whether the right\n  policy is retry-then-fail or retry-then-skip depends on what the diagnostic shows the\n  cause to be; default to **retry-then-fail** so a genuine misconfiguration still reds the\n  lane rather than silently skipping coverage.\n\n## Scope\n\n* `tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_fixtures.py` — the `dc_store_copy_repo` fixture's fetch\n  and archive calls.\n\n## Testing\n\n* **unit / fixture-level**: a fake `subprocess.run` that fails the fetch once then succeeds\n  proves the retry path; one that always fails proves the raised error text contains git's\n  stderr and the remote/branch, not just the exit status.\n* **live**: the next Live External Integration run shows\n  `test_outbound_unassign_round_trips` no longer erroring at setup — or, if it still does,\n  the log now names the actual git failure, which is the point.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] the fixture's `git fetch origin tickets` failure path raises an error whose message\n      contains git's captured stderr plus the remote and branch, verified by a fixture-level\n      test with a stubbed failing `subprocess.run`\n- [ ] the fetch retries a transient failure a bounded number of times before failing, proven\n      by a stub that fails once then succeeds\n- [ ] no cell is deleted, skipped or `xfail`ed to reach green\n- [ ] a Live External Integration run shows `test_outbound_unassign_round_trips` either\n      passing or failing with a message that names git's actual reason\n\n## Not in scope\n\nThe other residual in the same run —\n`test_dc_mutations.py::test_outbound_create_stamps_both_provenance_markers` failing with\n`rebar create failed (exit 1): Error: git commit failed while holding lock: git timed out\nafter 30s` — is the tracker write-lock contention family and is already tracked by\n`royal-weariless-zebrafish` (`10c3-5a33-2e25-4584`). Do not fold it in here.","id":"00c6-e96e-3f04-434d","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"DC store-copy fixture hard-fails on git fetch origin tickets and swallows git's stderr"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786533743895115001,"uuid":"cf5b6f47-85ed-4e3b-9a45-206c5041056c"}